SUMMARY:Rapp Lecture on Contemporary Art: Lotus L. Kang and Ebony L. Hayne
 s (Free)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n( WINNER of the 2026 Sobey Art Award )
 \n\n**EVENT is now Sold-Out**\n\n*The Rapp Lecture on Contemporary Art fea
 tures distinguished international leaders in the contemporary art world\, 
 including artists\, curators\, critics\, and scholars. The program was est
 ablished in 2009 in honour of Carol and Morton Rapp.*\n\n***PLEASE reserve
  your own FREE ticket*** in advance at the AGO link below.\n\n**Join artis
 t Lotus L. Kang and curator Ebony L. Haynes as they discuss Kang’s multi
 -disciplinary creative practice. They’ll explore how Kang uses unstable 
 and light-sensitive materials to consider the relationship between the bod
 y and its environments\, and how Haynes’ groundbreaking work leading New
  York’s 52 Walker Gallery led to them working together.**\n\nLotus Kang 
 is also short-listed for the upcoming Sobey Art Award. We'll visit her wor
 ks at the National Gallery in Ottawa--on our upcoming trip.\n\nhttps://www
 .gallery.ca/whats-on/sobey-art-award\n\n**Lotus L. Kang** is a New York-ba
 sed artist whose practice spans sculpture\, photography\, and site-respons
 ive installation. Recent solo exhibitions include the Bvlgari Pavilion at 
 the 61st Venice Biennale\, Frye Art Museum\, 52 Walker\, and Chisenhale Ga
 llery. Her work has also been featured in the Whitney Biennial\, Shanghai 
 Biennial\, and New Museum Triennial\, and is held in major museum collecti
 ons including the Art Gallery of Ontario\, Stedelijk Museum\, Whitney Muse
 um of American Art\, The Guggenheim Museum\, and Museum of Modern Art\, Ne
 w York.\n\n3 mins intro..\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NK00tdA5Qas\n
 \n**Ebony L. Haynes** is a New York-based curator and is the Global Head o
 f Curatorial Projects at David Zwirner. She previously led the gallery’s
  52 Walker space in Tribeca\, NY. Haynes sits on the boards of Artists Spa
 ce (New York)\, Topical Cream\, and the New Art Dealers Alliance. She also
  runs Black Art Sessions: an online school that offers free professional p
 ractice classes to Black students worldwide.\n\n**Reserve your own FREE ti
 cket here:**\n\nhttps://ago.ca/events/rapp-lecture-contemporary-art-lotus-
 l.-kang-and-ebony-l.-haynes\n\nNote--this ticket gets you into the AGO (fo
 r FREE) from 6pm onwards.
