SUMMARY:Hot Docs:  Tomson Highway--Permanent Astonishment ($20-$22)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n**Join us at Hot Docs--for a night wit
 h Tomson Highway**! New Documentary.\n(Note: this is a special screening--
 and NOT reserved seating--General admission)\n\n\\*\\*\\*Since *The Rez Si
 sters* premiered in Toronto in 1986\, **Tomson Highway** has gifted the wo
 rld with a multitude of award-winning plays\, musicals\, books\, and conce
 rts inspired by the people and places he’s encountered during his seven 
 decades of life.\n\nFrom his birth in a tent in Northern Manitoba to the p
 remiere of his latest play\, *Rose*\, at the National Arts Centre\, his ex
 traordinary life is captured in the documentary\, ***Tomson Highway: Perma
 nent Astonishment***.\n\n***Trailer:*** https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gz
 glG-cwGmU&t=162s\n\nDirected by Cree-Métis filmmaker Barbara Todd Hager\,
  the film explores Tomson’s Cree-influenced view of life\, his love of l
 aughter\, his family origins\, and how his plays launched an Indigenous th
 eatre movement in Canada.\n\n**Includes post-screening Q&A with special gu
 ests!!**\n\nhttps://ictnews.org/news/permanent-astonishment-new-documentar
 y-celebrates-the-life-and-work-of-canadas-most-celebrated-indigenous-write
 r/\n\nThis is a special screening. General admission. Premiere.\n\nhttps:/
 /tomsonhighway.ca/\n\n**Ticket link here: $20-$22**\n\nhttps://boxoffice.h
 otdocs.ca/websales/pages/info.aspx?evtinfo=641947\\~cf285ddd-dacb-4f18-89b
 8-1252c6dcffa6&epguid=a2104450-7e47-4369-a17d-c247570c3939&mdy=1/13/2027&s
 howing=641974&
